cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Adult-onset offending and arrest in Add Health: analysis code"
message: "If you use this code, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bowen
    given-names: Donald
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3527-9462"
    email: don@cemresearchlab.com
    website: "https://www.cemresearchlab.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/donbowen0-creator/REPLACE-WITH-REPO-NAME"
url: "https://www.cemresearchlab.com"
abstract: >-
  R code that builds the analysis files and estimates every model reported in a
  study of adult-onset offending and first arrest, using the public-use data of
  the National Longitudinal Study of Adolescent to Adult Health (Add Health),
  ICPSR 21600. The data themselves are not included and must be obtained from
  ICPSR.
keywords:
  - criminology
  - adult-onset offending
  - arrest
  - survival analysis
  - Add Health
  - R
